{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>ויאכל</b> — four times in the Masorah: ויאכל את כל עשב, קום אבי ויאכל, קראן לו ויאכל לחם, ויאכל לחם — regarding the false prophet who brought back the man of Elohim who came from Judah. ויאכל פרי מגדיו teaches that the locusts ate every choice fruit. Jethro, who was in that same counsel — because he fled and fed Moses, he was saved from it. Likewise the false prophet — because he fed the man of Elohim, he merited that HaShem spoke with him. Likewise Esau — because he came to feed his father, he merited and was blessed."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:23.422364148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}